note('thm-l1-stability-and-smooth-data-error','The L1 error theorem gives a sufficient C2-data estimate of order2-alpha; it explicitly disclaims uniformity as alpha approaches1.',empty='N:N>=1 gives a positive mesh and a nonempty set of positive-time equations.',one='C:For n=1 the sum over earlier cells in Proof4.1 is empty and the last-cell kernel estimate alone applies.',degenerate='N:T>0,N>=1 ensure h>0;0<alpha<1 keeps the Gamma/kernel factors finite.',endpoints='C:Proof4.2 fixes E^0=0; Proof4.1 treats the terminal singular cell by its exact power integral, and the maximum includes final timeT.')
note('lem-cq-quadratic-generating-coefficient-estimate','The coefficient lemma bounds one explicitly defined Taylor coefficient family; it makes no converse asymptotic criterion.',empty='N:The coefficient index n is at least1; s_1 is assigned before the two-term formula for n>=2.',one='C:s_1=1 is explicit, and Proof3.1 covers n=1,2 by enlarging the finite constant rather than using c_-1.',degenerate='N:alpha lies strictly in(0,1), so beta=2-alpha lies in(1,2) and all displayed positive Gamma denominators are defined.',endpoints='C:Proof1.1 handles z=0 separately and otherwise uses0<|z|<1; no convergence on z=1 is asserted.',choice='N:Proof3.1 enlarges one scalar constant to cover two explicitly finite cases; it does not choose a sequence of constants.')
note('thm-backward-euler-cq-scalar-resolvent-stability','The scalar CQ theorem proves unique updates, a stability bound and exact full-history counts, not a converse stability criterion.',empty='N:N>=1 gives at least one forcing value and a nonempty maximum over positive indices.',one='C:With N=1 the only convolution term multiplies V^0=0, and the counts in Proof2.1 become1 term and2 stored values.',degenerate='N:T>0,N>=1 imply h>0;lambda=0 is allowed because h^(-alpha)>0 remains in the diagonal.',endpoints='C:Proof1.1 initializes V^0=0; Proof4.1 uses n<=N to obtain h(n+1)<=2T, including n=N.',choice='C:Proof3.1 chooses the least maximising index from the finite nonzero sequence; the M=0 branch precedes that finite choice.')
note('thm-backward-euler-cq-compatible-quadratic-first-order-error','The quadratic CQ theorem proves first order for the compatible trajectory u_0+t^2, not for arbitrary nonsmooth data.',empty='N:The CQ grid inherited from its algorithm has N>=1; the error maximum includes the initial node.',one='C:The n=1 residual uses the separate coefficient s_1=1 supplied by the coefficient lemma, so no negative predecessor occurs.',degenerate='N:The admitted grid has h=T/N>0 and0<alpha<1;lambda=0 remains permitted by the positive CQ diagonal.',endpoints='C:Proof2.1 verifies u prime(0)=0 from the one-sided quotient; Proof5.1 retains E^0=0 before the maximum bound.',choice='N:Proof4.1 obtains one explicit uniform residual coefficient from the fixed quadratic coefficient lemma; no unknown exact trajectory is selected.')
note('ex-l1-and-cq-fractional-relaxation-first-step','The relaxation example solves two specified first-step equations; it is not an iff statement about their later trajectories.',empty='N:A first step of width h>0 and the supplied initial value1 are explicitly required.',zero='N:h=0 is excluded; neither displayed inverse is claimed to be a fractional derivative at zero step width.',one='C:The entire example is the n=1 branch: its two scalar equations give the stated distinct inverse denominators.',degenerate='N:The example fixes alpha=1/2 and positive h, avoiding the excluded order/zero-step limits.',endpoints='C:Both calculations start at U^0=1 and return positive U^1<1; no long-time endpoint conclusion is asserted.',choice='N:Verification1.1 and2.1 solve explicit positive scalar equations; no nonlinear root selection is involved.')
note('ex-l1-full-history-cost-and-truncation-bias','The L1 memory example computes counts and one exact bias for u=t; it supplies no converse accuracy guarantee.',empty='C:For zero retained increments m=0 the retained sum is empty and its value0 agrees with (mh)^(1-alpha)/Gamma(2-alpha).',zero='C:Verification2.1 telescopes the empty m=0 sum to0; for n<=m no increment is omitted.',one='C:At N=1 the direct-history count is1, and at m=1 each later truncated sum retains its single latest increment.',degenerate='N:The fractional-grid setting retains h>0 and0<alpha<1; a zero time step is not a truncation option.',endpoints='C:Verification3.1 states that m=N makes every step full-history and its bias zero.',choice='N:The retained lags are explicitly j=0,...,m-1, and Verification1.3 counts them by a finite reindexing.')
