note('def-local-leapfrog-domain-on-an-open-configuration-set','The local leapfrog item defines a restriction of three supplied shears to admitted configurations, not an iff symplecticity theorem.',empty='C:If Q is empty there are no admitted states and the local restriction has empty domain; no output or flow completeness is asserted.',one='C:For one configuration coordinate, the admitted-set condition still checks q and q+b M^(-1)p in the same open subset of R.',degenerate='N:The mass matrix is symmetric positive definite, so a singular mass matrix is outside the specified domain.',endpoints='N:Q is open and the procedure is restricted to interior admitted states; there is no closed time-interval endpoint condition.',choice='N:The intermediate configurations are the explicit kick/drift formulas; the admitted set is their stated domain restriction.')
note('lem-local-hamiltonian-flow-preserves-symplectic-matrix','The Hamiltonian flow lemma proves Y transpose J Y=J for an existing local flow; it does not characterize all symplectic maps as such flows.',zero='C:At time0 the variational initial value is Y(0)=I, and Proof2.1 gives I transpose J I=J.',one='C:For one degree of freedom J is the2-by-2 canonical matrix, and the same symmetric-Hessian calculation applies.',degenerate='C:A zero Hessian gives A=0 in Proof1.1, so the variational matrix is constant and the identity still holds.',endpoints='N:The conclusion is limited to times on the admitted local trajectory; no global terminal-time existence is inferred.',choice='N:Proof2.1 differentiates the already given variational solution Y(t); the Statement explicitly describes the proof as local and choice-free.')
note('alg-local-symplectic-euler-step','The kick-then-drift algorithm fixes a partial update and its failure statuses, not an equivalence between residual tolerance and symplecticity.',empty='N:A supplied admitted state(q,p) is required; no update is called on an empty state list.',zero='N:The algorithm input requires h>0; its mathematical signed-zero extension is not its admitted step-size branch.',one='C:For d=1 the update is p_plus=p-h V prime(q), followed by q_plus=q+h p_plus/M.',degenerate='N:A singular M is excluded by positive definiteness; a trial outside Q returns domain-failure rather than a successful degenerate step.',endpoints='N:The configuration domain is open; membership is checked on the actual trial q_plus rather than imposed as boundary data.',choice='N:Both update coordinates are explicit, and uncertifiable finite evaluation returns inconclusive.')
note('alg-implicit-midpoint-hamiltonian-step','Implicit midpoint defines a certified local root branch and finite Picard output certificates; it does not equate approximate output with exact symplecticity.',empty='C:An update budget B=0 returns the supplied stage z and output-error bound2rho before any Picard update.',one='C:For B=1 the algorithm forms Z_1 once, tests radius2 theta d_1/(1-theta), and otherwise returns inconclusive.',degenerate='C:At theta=0 the rule uses theta^k=0 only for k>=1 and never evaluates0^0.',endpoints='C:The certificate allows |h|M/2=rho but requires theta<1; unavailable balls and bounds have separate failure statuses.',choice='N:The exact branch is the locally unique root in the supplied ball, while finite iterates start deterministically at z.')
note('lem-canonical-kick-and-drift-shears-have-symplectic-jacobians','The shear lemma verifies a block-matrix symplectic identity under C2 and positive-mass hypotheses; it states no converse regularity criterion.',empty='C:On an empty open configuration domain there are no admitted points and the pointwise derivative claim is vacuous.',zero='C:Setting a=0 in Proof1.1 or b=0 in Proof1.2 gives an identity shear with Jacobian I.',one='C:In d=1 the two block calculations reduce to scalar lower and upper triangular shear matrices with determinant1.',degenerate='C:A zero Hessian or zero shear parameter makes the corresponding off-diagonal block zero; no Hessian invertibility is needed.',endpoints='N:The derivative claim is on each open admitted domain, with no closed-boundary derivative assumed.',choice='N:Proof1.1 and1.2 explicitly differentiate the kick and drift and multiply the resulting blocks.')
note('prop-local-leapfrog-and-symplectic-euler-are-symplectic','The composition proposition proves symplectic Jacobians for two admitted methods, not exact conservation of the original energy or an iff theorem.',empty='C:If the admitted domain is empty there is no composed point to differentiate, so the pointwise assertion is vacuous.',zero='C:Identity shear factors at a zero signed parameter preserve the product identity in Proof2.1.',one='C:Proof2.1 applies unchanged to2-by-2 shear matrices for one degree of freedom.',degenerate='C:The only required matrices are the admitted shear Jacobians; a zero potential curvature is allowed in their product.',endpoints='N:Proof1.1 requires every intermediate configuration in open Q, without an extension to boundary points.',choice='N:The two compositions have respectively three and two fixed factors; the chain-rule product involves no selected intermediate branch.')
note('thm-local-symplectic-euler-and-leapfrog-trajectory-errors','The trajectory theorem proves orders1 and2 on a controlled compact tube; it does not infer unconditional admissibility from symplecticity.',empty='N:N>=1 and T>0 give a nonempty time partition; the initial state also makes the stipulated comparison tube nonempty.',zero='C:At n=0 the error bound includes the supplied initial error e_0 before any recurrence increment.',one='C:Proof2.1 and2.2 give the single-step defects h^2 and h^3; Proof3.1 also applies when there is only one update.',degenerate='N:Positive-definite M and the explicit tube/derivative bounds exclude a singular mass or leaving the admitted configuration domain.',endpoints='C:The finite recurrence includes every nh<=T, including n=N; the compact tube must contain all associated intermediate states.',choice='N:The compared trajectories and methods are fixed; Proof3.1 iterates a finite deterministic error inequality.')
note('thm-implicit-midpoint-branch-symplectic-order-and-error','The midpoint theorem separates its C2 contraction result from C3 exact-map symplecticity and trajectory estimates; no converse or finite-output symplecticity is claimed.',empty='N:The declared closed ball contains its supplied center z and is therefore nonempty.',zero='C:Proof1.1 states the theta=0 constant-map branch, gives Z_1=Z and vanishing b_k for k>=1; h=0 also gives the identity map.',one='C:At k=1 the stage error is at most theta times d_1 divided by1-theta, and the output error is twice that bound.',degenerate='C:The zero-contraction case is handled before division by any iterate error; only1-theta appears in the error denominator.',endpoints='C:Proof1.1 permits equality in |h|M/2<=rho and separately enforces strict theta<1, including the k=0 error convention.')
note('lem-finite-modified-hamiltonian-exists','The finite logarithm theorem constructs Hamiltonian coefficients through a fixed N; it explicitly asserts no convergence of an infinite modified series.',zero='C:The formal pullback has P_0=I; division by h in the Statement denotes a finite formal coefficient shift, not a numerical evaluation at h=0.',one='C:For symplectic Euler r=1,N=1 the finite recursion supplies only X_1,H_1; r=2 methods still require N>=2.',degenerate='N:The star center lies in Q and M is positive definite; a non-star-shaped domain or singular mass is not an admitted global-primitive setting.',endpoints='C:Proof4.1 integrates the radial primitive from0 to1, whose boundary term at0 vanishes and at1 equals the specified one-form.')
note('lem-truncated-modified-flow-matches-map','The matching lemma bounds two maps with identical coefficients through degreeN+1, rather than characterizing all high-order methods.',empty='O:The Statement permits a compact K without explicit nonemptiness while displaying a real supremum over K; the intended empty-domain supremum convention needs confirmation before an empty-axis discharge.',zero='C:At h=0 both method and comparison flow are the identity, so their difference and the displayed error bound vanish.',one='C:For r=N=1 the matched coefficients run through h^2 and the remainder estimate is C_1|h|^3.',degenerate='N:The result is conditional on admitted map/flow branches and compact K prime inside U; it does not continue a branch outside that domain.',endpoints='C:The displayed estimate includes |h|<=h_0 on either sign of time, with both trajectories remaining in the controlled tube.',choice='N:Proof1.1 fixes the already constructed modified field, and Proof2.1 bounds the two Taylor remainders rather than choosing new coefficients.')
note('lem-finite-modified-hamiltonian-close-to-original','The finite coefficient bound shows O(h^r) closeness for fixed N; it does not claim a converse or convergence as N increases.',zero='N:The displayed scalar estimate is stated for0<h<=1; its proof does not divide by h or require a zero-step modified evolution.',one='C:Proof1.1 uses h^j<=h^r for0<h<=1, with equality at h=1 for every coefficient.',degenerate='N:The coefficient functions are those of the already admitted smooth modified-Hamiltonian construction; no singular mass extension is made.',endpoints='C:The upper step-size endpoint h=1 is explicitly included in Proof1.1.',choice='N:The constant C_0 is the sum of finitely many coefficient suprema fixed by the existing H_j; it is not chosen by an approximation algorithm.')
note('lem-one-step-modified-energy-defect','The defect lemma gives an upper bound for one admitted step relative to a fixed modified flow, not an equivalence with exact numerical energy conservation.',empty='N:The specified z and the comparison endpoints all lie in K prime, so its comparison tube contains an actual state.',zero='N:The theorem is stated for sufficiently small0<h<=1; it does not require evaluating a zero-step defect formula.',one='C:The whole assertion is a single-step energy bound; for the r=N=1 branch it bounds that defect by C_1 h^2.',degenerate='N:The endpoint comparison segment must remain in K prime inside U; no boundary-crossing or missing-flow branch is admitted.',endpoints='C:Proof2.1 bounds the gradient on the entire segment joining the method and modified-flow endpoints, not just their initial state.',choice='N:Proof1.1 uses the specified local flow and Proof2.1 fixes C_1=G_N C_N from the existing two bounds.')
note('thm-finite-order-modified-energy-bound','The theorem bounds the original energy by endpoint modification plus accumulated finite defect; it disclaims exact conservation and infinite-series convergence.',empty='C:At n=0 the increment sum in Proof1.1 is empty and z_n=z_0, so the left-hand energy difference is zero.',zero='C:Zero step count n=0 is explicitly admitted; Proof2.1 then bounds the identical endpoint energies without an update.',one='C:For n=1 the telescoping sum has one defect and gives2C_0 h^r+C_1 h^(N+1).',degenerate='N:An admitted fixed method, positive h and a common compact tube are required; a domain exit is outside this finite-time energy guarantee.',endpoints='C:Proof2.1 compares both z_0 and z_n to their modified Hamiltonian values, retaining two endpoint-error terms.',choice='N:The coefficient orderN and method are fixed inputs; Proof1.1 sums precisely the given n numerical increments.')
note('ex-backward-euler-is-a-stable-but-not-symplectic','The example proves A-stability and failure of oscillator symplecticity for h>0; it asserts no equivalence between those two properties.',empty='N:The example fixes a two-coordinate oscillator state, not an empty input list.',zero='N:Its nonsymplecticity conclusion assumes h>0; at h=0 the identity matrix is not a claimed counterexample.',one='C:For one oscillator degree of freedom Proof2.1 computes the2-by-2 determinant1/(1+h^2).',degenerate='C:A zero oscillator state maps to itself, but the map determinant remains below1 for h>0, so zero state does not imply symplecticity.',endpoints='C:Proof1.1 includes Re(z)=0 in its half-plane stability inequality, since |1-z|^2>=1 there.',choice='N:Verification2.1 inverts an explicitly displayed2-by-2 matrix with denominator1+h^2>0.')
note('ex-stoermer-verlet-bounded-harmonic-oscillator-energy','The Verlet example proves an exact modified quadratic invariant and a sufficient uniform energy-error bound; it is not an iff characterization of stability.',empty='N:The oscillator has supplied coordinates(q,p), and the step-count assertion follows its fixed matrix powers.',zero='N:The positive-definite modified-energy claim explicitly assumes0<|h|<2; h=0 is not needed to divide by its step-dependent coefficient.',one='C:For one step, Verification2.1 directly establishes the invariant quadratic matrix equality.',degenerate='C:If the initial oscillator state is zero, the linear step leaves it zero and both modified/original energies vanish.',endpoints='N:The strict bound0<|h|<2 excludes |h|=2, where1-h^2/4 ceases to be positive.',choice='N:The invariant is an explicit quadratic form and Verification3.1 compares its two displayed endpoint values.')
note('ex-symplectic-euler-harmonic-oscillator','The oscillator example verifies symplecticity for every real h and separately exhibits nonconservation of H; it is not an equivalence of those properties.',empty='N:The oscillator state has two explicitly supplied coordinates.',zero='C:At h=0 the displayed matrix is I and the determinant computation still gives1.',one='C:For one degree of freedom Verification2.1 obtains determinant1, and Verification3.1 supplies a single-step energy increase.',degenerate='C:The zero state remains zero under the linear matrix, while the nonconservation witness instead uses(0,1).',endpoints='N:h ranges over all reals in the symplecticity claim; there is no finite step-size endpoint to extend.',choice='N:The counterexample state(q,p)=(0,1) is explicitly assigned and its energy difference is h^2/2.')
