note('lem-parabolic-bochner-time-mollification','The mollification lemma constructs smooth graph-norm approximants and a unique weak derivative; it is not an iff smoothness statement.',empty='N:The evolution interval has positiveT and the given u belongs to its energy space; the zero function is allowed rather than an absent input.',zero='C:If u=0 and its weak derivative is zero, every reflected convolution in Proof4.1 is zero.',one='C:For V=H=R, the reflection and Bochner integrals become their scalar counterparts without changing the argument.',degenerate='C:On a zero evolution space all representatives and convolutions are zero; no division by a vector norm occurs.',endpoints='C:Proof3.1 reflects evenly across0 andT and cancels seam terms, while epsilon<T/2 prevents the outer zero-extension jumps from entering the convolution.',choice='C:Countable Choice is an explicit hypothesis; Proof6.1 selects a countable epsilon sequence only after the reflection and convolution construction, retaining the assumption used by the approximation supplier.')
